{"keel_admission": "A-0001", "keel_component": "algebra", "date": "2026-07-30", "quarry_path": "algebra/", "carried_from": "472fc0a8", "carried_modules": ["cl41.py", "versor.py", "cga.py", "rotor.py", "null_point.py"], "status": "carried_not_retired", "surface_delta": 0, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 196, "test_files": 108}, "why_not_retired": "Nothing can be removed. 196 production modules and 108 test files in this repository import algebra, and the keel's copy serves nothing yet — it is admitted-but-unreached, which ADR-0006 defers rather than relaxes. Deleting or thinning algebra/ here would take the serving system down to shrink a number, which charter Article VII forbids: users lose nothing during migration.", "retires_when": "A keel consumer serves what depends on this layer. Concretely: K3 admits logos/, giving algebra a caller and closing articulation (iv)'s open consumer row; then the 196 consumers here migrate or retire in their own admissions, and algebra/ is deleted in the row that removes the last one.", "keel_evidence": {"articulations": "../coreai/docs/admissions/A-0001.md", "audit": "../coreai/docs/atlas/k1-algebra-quarry-audit.md", "ledger": "../coreai/data/admissions.jsonl", "byte_identity": "cl41 207540d3d1a1, versor 67f0c1932f66, cga 3b2425e65093, rotor 16f43e92087f, null_point 38becf1f8f87 (sha256 prefixes, verified against 472fc0a8)"}, "not_carried": {"backend.py": "rebuild — catches (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError, Exception) and passes, on the critical path of 52 import sites here (lessons ledger H-11). Stays serving; the keel will rebuild the dispatch rather than carry it.", "holonomy.py": "leave — FA-1 ruled the resonance claim NO-GO, so the job it does is not a job the keel has. Still has 3 production consumers here; retires with them.", "topological_reasoning/": "leave — already quarantined here, correctly, with its own blocklist. The keel cites it as the model shape for a deliberately-dark declaration."}, "protocol_not