{"keel_admission": "A-0003", "keel_component": "logos", "date": "2026-07-30", "quarry_path": "packs/ vocab/ morphology/ alignment/ evals/logos/", "carried_from": "069ceb55", "superseded_modules": {"packs/compiler.py": {"lines": 662, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 39, "test_files": 29}}, "packs/schema.py": {"lines": 202, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 12, "test_files": 4}}, "vocab/manifold.py": {"lines": 302, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 13, "test_files": 6}}, "alignment/graph.py": {"lines": 99, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 5, "test_files": 1}}, "morphology/registry.py": {"lines": 97, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 4, "test_files": 2}}}, "status": "carried_not_retired", "surface_delta": 0, "consumers_here": {"production_modules": 162, "test_files": 86, "note": "importers of `packs` as a whole; the per-module counts above are the ones that must migrate before deletion"}, "classification": "rebuild", "why_not_retired": "Same shape as A-0001 and for the same reason: the keel's logos serves nothing yet — it is the top of the admitted stack and its own consumer (perception/L4) does not exist, recorded as an ADR-0007 deferral with `awaiting: perception`. 162 production modules here import `packs`. Article VII forbids taking the serving system down to shrink a number.", "retires_when": "K4 admits the reader, giving logos a caller; then the 162 consumers here migrate or retire in their own admissions, and these five modules are deleted in the row that removes the last one.", "what_the_keel_will_not_take": {"the domain overlays": "units, numerics, frames, compositions, ethics, safety, identity, register, rhetorical style, primitives, anchor lens, vision, audio, sensorimotor (~3,900 lines). Each is governed by a `Proposed` record (ADR-0084, ADR-0128, ADR-0168, ADR-0169) or has no keel consumer. Step 2b, recorded per-field in ../coreai/data/pack_declarations.json.", "the domain-contract fields": "domain_contract_version, domain_id, axioms, rules, teaching_chains, eval_lanes, reviewers, known_gaps — carried by all four depth packs in the logos mount. Authority is CLEAN (ADR-0091/0092/0093 accepted); excluded because packs/domain_contract.py has no keel consumer and a manifest field the keel neither validates nor reads is testimony, not evidence.", "the pack-authoring tools": "en_seeder.py, compile_pack.py, compile_frames.py, compile_compositions.py, __main__.py (~700 lines). The keel compiles from committed, sealed data; the tools that produce packs are not part of the ground.", "evals/logos/fa1_gate.py": "leave — the experiment is run, closed and recorded. Its tripwires already live here (tests/test_fa1_gate_verdict.py, tests/test_holonomy_resonance.py) and stay.", "chat/pack_grounding.py's raw-path lexicon read": "banned, not carried. It opens en_collapse_anchors_v1/lexicon.jsonl directly, bypassing the loader that refuses that pack. This is the one-loader violation the keel's pack door exists to make impossible."}, "carried_repairs": {"evals/logos/repaired_ground.py": "geodesic_blend and mount-wide edge resolution, written here against the real compile path during FA-1 and carried into the keel's compiler proper rather than left as an eval-time monkey-patch.", "evals/logos/manifold_collapse.py": "the bit-exact collision census, promoted from an eval instrument to a build gate: the keel's Ground refuses a colliding coordinate at construction, so there is no census to remember to run."}, "withdrawn_at_admission": {"count": 24, "what": "alignment edges whose target_id is owned by en_collapse_anchors_v1, in he_core_cognition_v1 (10) and grc_logos_cognition_v1 (14)", "why": "The pack declares role 'collapse_anchor' and oov_policy 'passthrough', neither of which is a member of any registry — it has been formally unloadable since it landed and served only through the raw-path bypass above. Declaring two vocabulary rows to legitimise it would widen a registry to fit a defect; its real caller, ADR-0073's anchor-lens machinery, is L5/L6 and does not exist in the keel. Decided 2026-07-30 by Shay under Article VIII. THE EDGES ARE NOT DELETED HERE — this repository keeps all 83; the keel carries 59.", "readmit_when": "a keel phase admits the anchor lens with a caller"}, "keel_evidence": {"articulations": "../coreai/docs/admissions/A-0003.md", "audit": "../coreai/docs/atlas/k3-logos-quarry-audit.md", "ledger": "../coreai/data/admissions.jsonl", "re_derived_here_not_believed": "6/6 lexicon seals recomputed from the carried bytes and matching; 397 entries -> 397 distinct coordinates bit-exact (this repository's shipped compiler: 353 -> 300, 53 lost across 25 groups); 59 of 59 carried edges resolve (here: 20 of 83); 300 lawful operators belonging to no pack identify as nothing, where an argmax over the same 300 answers every time onto 85 distinct entries with one taking 22."}, "what_the_run_found_that_reading_did_not": "The keel's mount compiles 397 lexical entries; packs/compiler.py's ground holds 353. The 44 missing ones are dropped by `if surface in seen: continue` in _load_mounted_packs_cached, and ALL 44 disagree with the row that shadows them — different semantic_domains, therefore different coordinates. Which curation survives depends on mount order. en_minimal_v1 declares `will` twice (en-044, a NOUN of agency/divine agency; en-176, an AUX of tense/modality): two words sharing a spelling, which a surface-keyed ground cannot hold. All 397 entry_ids are distinct and all 118 endpoints of the alignment corpus are entry_ids — the alignment graph already spoke the right key and only the ground did not. This is a live defect in THIS repository, not merely a keel design note: 44 curated entries are silently unreachable in every mounted configuration served here.", "protocol_note": "Second consecutive admission with surface_delta 0, for the same structural reason A-0001 recorded: a bottom-up sequence admits a layer long before anything consumes it. A-0001's `retires_when` named 'K3 admits logos/, giving algebra a caller' as its first condition — that condition is now MET (../coreai import graph: logos -> [algebra, contracts]), and A-0001's status still does not flip, because nothing has been deleted here. Reaching a layer in the keel is not shrinking a surface here, and conflating the two would make the ratchet report progress it has not made."}
